  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The CONSOLE font, and only the console font.

         This is a bitmap atlas generated with the XDK's FontMaker from
         Selawik, Microsoft's openly-licensed (SIL OFL) metric-compatible
         stand-in for Segoe UI. See Media/Fonts/OFL.txt for the license and
         copyright notice, which the OFL requires be distributed with it.

         It used to draw the whole UI. It no longer does: UiText.cpp renders
         the UI through XUI, straight from selawk.ttf, which removed both of
         this atlas's limits - a fixed strike size that made small text soft,
         and a character range stopping at 0x7F that blanked the trademark
         sign in real title names.

         What still needs it is ATG::Console, which draws dprintf output via
         "embed:\font" before the UI is initialised. That is the path a very
         early failure reports itself on, so it has to work without XUI being
         up, which is exactly why this stays.

         Named uifont_16 rather than Selawik_16 on purpose. Selawik ships
         "with Reserved Font Name Selawik", and OFL 1.1 defines a Modified
         Version to include a derivative made "by changing formats or by
         porting the Font Software to a new environment" - which is what
         converting the TTF to an ATG .abc/.tga atlas is. Clause 3 then bars a
         Modified Version from using the reserved name. Saying what it derives
         from, as this comment does, is fine; naming the generated files after
         it is not. selawk.ttf itself is unmodified, so it keeps its name. -->
    <CustomBuild Include="Media\Fonts\uifont_16.rdf">
      <FileType>Document</FileType>
      <Command Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|Xbox 360'">bundler "%(FullPath)" -o "$(OutDir)Media\Fonts\font.xpr"</Command>
      <Outputs Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|Xbox 360'">$(OutDir)Media\Fonts\font.xpr</Outputs>
    </CustomBuild>
